    "body": "With regard to XFO: I didn't do any additional research beyond getting a count. It's something that's broken applications in the past (both Google Drive and Dropbox both served XFO on redirect responses that were expected to turn into downloads, AFAIR), and given that experience, it didn't seem worth the time it would take to dive into HTTP Archive and/or add additional metrics to track things down more closely. I'd welcome analysis that showed it to be less likely to break things than my priors suggest.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
